<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Shenzong of Song</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1048">1048</a>–<a href="/years/1085">1085</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Shenzong</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emperor Shenzong was an emperor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Northern Song</a> in the late eleventh century. He backed the reforms of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-anshi">Wang Anshi</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-policies-song">New Policies</a>, which aimed to strengthen state finances and the military of the Song Dynasty but provoked intense factional opposition.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-shenzong-of-song.jpg" alt="Emperor Shenzong of Song" width="278" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shenzong.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The reversal of the reforms after Emperor <b>Shenzong</b>'s death in 1085 illustrated the bitter factional struggle between reformers and conservatives that consumed enormous political energy through the late Northern Song.</blockquote><a href="/empire/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>In practice he governed with his ministers: when Emperor <b>Shenzong</b> said in 1071 that the New Policies were meant to benefit the people, his minister Wen Yanbo replied that the emperor governed with the officials, not with the people.</blockquote><a href="/societies/song-china">Social Hierarchy of Song China</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaifeng">Kaifeng</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/china">China</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaifeng">Kaifeng</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/china">China</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=34.8,114.35&amp;year=1072" aria-label="Kaifeng on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7451 904 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Emperor Shenzong of Song"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7901 1174h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7901 1174h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=34.8,114.35&amp;year=1072">What was here in 1072? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
